    parts=['# Additional research: which unused indicators confirm an early rise?\n\nStudy UPTREND-EXTENSION-20261029 · completed2026-10-29 · KR and US separately · offline research only.\n']
    parts.append('## Answer\n\n**The additional indicators did not replace the established early-confirmation tradeoff.** RMI30 was the strongest new candidate on early precision, but its TEST precision was20.1% in Korea and23.8% in the US, below the unchanged MACD+RSI benchmark at31.1% and34.8%. It also captured fewer eligible starts and arrived slightly later. SAR and StochRSI covered more starts than MACD+RSI, but the existing CCI recovery condition had both higher precision and higher capture in both markets.\n\nThe useful new finding is the separation between **early recognition, recognition of an ongoing rise, and subsequent price information**. Supertrend classified completed rising periods much better than it located their first six days. TRIX zero-crossing was especially late. Some of these late signals retained favorable21-day associations in restricted matched samples; that does not make them early-confirmation signals or validated profitable entry rules.\n\nThis extension evaluated8 new families /11 events plus5 unchanged benchmark events, without changing the original L1 labels. The dates have already been studied: all TEST findings are **exploratory historical reassessment**, not a new independent holdout.\n')
