    parts.append(table(['Signal','KR whole% / base%','US whole% / base%','Late% KR / US','Early/down-flat event-rate ratio KR / US'],rows))
    parts.append('Supertrend’s whole-up accuracy is85.5% in both markets, but roughly77–78% of **all** its alerts are late confirmations. Its early precision is not clearly above the early base after this wave’s simultaneous adjustment. TRIX-zero’s early precision is0.14%/0.21%, even though whole-up precision is76.1%/78.0%. This is direct evidence that a good ongoing-trend indicator can be unsuitable for the requested first-six-day task.\n\nThe early/down-flat event-rate ratio can also mislead if read alone: Supertrend’s ratio is5.36/4.18, because it rarely fires during down/flat labels. That comparison leaves out the many late-uptrend alerts. Precision lift against **all eligible dates** is only1.25/1.06. Use both measures, and do not replace the all-signal denominator with the days already labeled up.\n\nNew RMI30, SAR, both StochRSI events, Chaikin and volume oscillator are concentrated above their early bases after this fixed-family correction in both markets. US AVWAP also is; KR AVWAP is uncertain. Statistical concentration alone does not make the lower-precision candidates preferable to the existing benchmarks.\n')
