    parts.append('RMI adds only3.0/3.5pp of episode coverage beyond CCI; SAR adds8.3/10.6pp; StochRSI K20 adds7.5/8.9pp. Relative to the more selective MACD+RSI, RMI adds9.1/10.6pp and StochRSI adds39.1/43.1pp. The “either” column is an overlap diagnostic, **not a tested OR alert’s precision or a recommendation to combine signals**. More alerts also bring non-early alerts. All new/benchmark pairs, including SMA5, are in '+link('episode-overlap.csv')+'.\n\nNo new simultaneous/order/persistence filters were fitted in this extension. Prior research already documented their precision-versus-delay/capture cost. The fixed current question was whether these individual mechanisms offered useful additional recognition; the predeclared wave stopped there.\n')
    parts.append('## What happened after ALL signals?\n\nThe next valid contiguous open is the reference price. Touches and favorable/adverse excursions use highs/lows over the next21 bars inclusive; terminal return uses close at bar21. MFE is maximum favorable excursion and MAE is positive adverse depth. Both are averages of path extrema, **not earned returns**. The following focus set includes new early candidates, late-trend contrasts and the two prior anchors; all16 events at5/21/63 bars are in '+link('path-distributions.csv')+'.\n')
    focal=['rmi30','psar','stochrsi20','supertrend','trix_zero','macd_rsi40','cci_recovery']
