    parts.append(table(['Market','Signal','All-signal N','+5% touch%','−5% touch%','Mean MFE%','Mean MAE%','Mean end%','Median end%','End p10 / p90%'],rows))
    parts.append('Both a +5% and a −5% touch can occur on one path; their probabilities do not sum to100%. Means can be driven by the long right tail, especially in the US universe. Medians, quantiles, minima/maxima and positive-terminal probabilities are retained without outcome-based trimming. These are adjusted-price paths and do not include a complete execution/cost/dividend model.\n\nFor comparison, the hindsight **early-hit subset** looks much better. It is useful for describing already-correct confirmations, but is invalid as the primary test of the live signal’s future information.\n')
    rows=[]
