    parts.append('- '+link('results-and-code.zip','Results, charts, documentation and code ZIP')+'\n- '+link('primary-summary.csv','Main32-row results')+' · '+link('KR-signal-definitions.csv','KR conditions')+' · '+link('US-signal-definitions.csv','US conditions')+'\n- '+link('protocol-receipt.json','Pre-calculation hash/time receipt')+' · '+link('verification-extension.json','Benchmark/overlap verification')+' · '+link('verification-report.json','Report/figure/link verification')+'\n- [Reproduction instructions and code](../../scripts/research/uptrend_extension/README.md)\n- [Full compressed per-signal ledger](../../runtime/uptrend-extension-20261029/all-signal-ledger.csv.gz), with date, label, reference-related fields and all5/21/63-bar outcomes. Price inputs/per-stock statistics stay in the separate new runtime.\n\nThe bundle is self-contained for reading and inspecting results; recomputation additionally requires the identical archived input caches. The frozen source hashes and provenance are supplied rather than pretending the bundle contains all raw market history.\n')
    parts.append('## Conclusion and stopping decision\n\n**Confirmed within this historical definition:** the new events show distinct timing roles. RMI30 is more selective than most new candidates but inferior to MACD+RSI for early precision and capture here. SAR and StochRSI broaden recognition relative to MACD+RSI, while existing CCI recovery provides the stronger pooled early-coverage tradeoff. StochRSI low K/D is faster at the cost of more false early confirmations. Supertrend/TRIX predominantly confirm an already-established rise.\n\n**Still uncertain:** future generalization, point-in-time corporate-action behavior, delisted-stock performance, live platform equivalence, and whether restricted matched path associations survive a genuinely new period and an execution/cost/exit specification. TRIX-zero’s better-balanced positive path association is worth retaining as a separate ongoing-trend hypothesis, not converting into a conclusion about early recognition.\n\n**Practical scope:** these signals can prompt a closer examination of a recovery or an ongoing trend. They do not certify the label in real time, and they do not establish that buying the signal earns an excess net return. A useful analogy is a train-departure detector: a device that correctly says the train is moving may usually ring long after departure. Early precision asks whether the ring came in the first six bars; capture asks how many departures it noticed; the subsequent journey is a separate measurement.\n\n**The requested historical early-confirmation question is sufficiently answered, so this fixed extension ends here.** More indicator/threshold searching on the same history is not required for this conclusion. A future study would be justified by a different decision—such as prospective ongoing-trend entry testing—not by an obligation to find a universal winning indicator. No automatic monitoring or trading implementation follows from this report.\n')
